{"kind":"stack","id":"magnets-poles","title":"Magnets: attract or repel?","theme":{"background":"#f4f7fb","foreground":"#1d2a3a","font":"Arial, sans-serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-t","content":"Magnetic poles"},{"type":"text","id":"c1-e","content":"Every magnet has two ends called poles: north and south."},{"type":"image","id":"c1-i","picto":"magnet"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Attract"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"Attract means two magnets pull towards each other. Opposite poles attract."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-b","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Two north poles are brought close together. What happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"They repel each other","why":"Like poles push apart, so the magnets repel.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"They attract each other","why":"Pupils mix up which pairing pulls together.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"They stick together","why":"Pupils think all magnets must stick.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-q","content":"A north pole is brought near a south pole. What happens?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"They attract each other","why":"Opposite poles pull towards each other.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"They repel each other","why":"Pupils mix up which pairing pushes apart.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-c","label":"Nothing happens","why":"Pupils forget that magnetic poles act at a distance.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-q","content":"You have two bar magnets. Which will you try first?"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-a","label":"Turn one magnet round","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c5-b","label":"Push the two magnets together as they are","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"You turn one magnet round. Now the magnets pull together. The opposite poles are facing."},{"type":"button","id":"c6-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-t","content":"You push them together and they push apart. The like poles are facing each other."},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-q","content":"Two south poles face each other. What will the magnets do?"},{"type":"button","id":"c8-a","label":"Repel each other","why":"Like poles, both south, push each other away.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-b","label":"Attract each other","why":"Pupils think any two poles pull together.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c8-c","label":"Stay still in the air","why":"Pupils think magnets need to touch to move.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"A north pole faces a north pole. Will they attract or repel?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Repel","why":"Like poles push each other away.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Attract","why":"Pupils think any two poles pull together.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which pair of poles will attract each other?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"North and south","why":"Opposite poles pull towards each other.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"North and north","why":"Pupils think two north poles should stick.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"South and south","why":"Pupils think two south poles should stick.","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-h","content":"Magnets finished!"},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Well done. You can now predict whether magnets will attract or repel."}],"actions":[]}}
